# The Sound kits and Add instrument dialogs. Ids start with "sounds-".
# Kit names come from the sound bank and are not translated.

# At the top of the list, when the SoundFont playing lacks the beat's kit. $kit is the kit the
# beat asks for; $played is the kit that plays instead.
sounds-kit-missing = This beat asks for { $kit }, which this SoundFont does not have. { $played } plays instead.
# Shows the bank's kits that are not in the short list, below it.
sounds-more-kits = More kits
# Hides them again.
sounds-fewer-kits = Fewer kits
# A few words under each kit of the short list, on how it sounds.
sounds-kit-standard = The usual kit, good for almost anything
sounds-kit-room = A kit in a room, with a little echo
sounds-kit-hiphop = Dry, deep sounds for hip-hop
sounds-kit-power = A big kick and snare, for rock
sounds-kit-electro = Electronic drums
sounds-kit-808 = The classic drum machine of hip-hop and electro
sounds-kit-dance = Electronic drums for dance music
sounds-kit-909 = The classic drum machine of house and techno
sounds-kit-jazz = A light, soft kit, for jazz
sounds-kit-brush = A snare played with brushes, for jazz and ballads
sounds-kit-orchestral = Timpani and orchestra percussion
sounds-max-rows = A project holds at most { $count } rows.
# Opens the drums that are not in the short list of common ones.
sounds-more-drums = More drums
# Hover text on a drum in Add instrument that already has a row. A right click or long press
# still plays it.
sounds-already-added = Already added. Right-click or long-press to hear it.
